target/
**/c_src/build/
Cargo.lock
**/build-ninja/
**/.cargo/
**/cc-wrapper.sh
**/linker-wrapper.sh
**/linker_wrapper.sh
**/test_vectors/
**/runner/
*.vsync
**/.git
**/gtest_build/
**/tests/*.so

# The agent-invocation cache (results/.cache/<SCHEMA>/) IS committed: it is what lets
# tools/reproduce.sh replay a battery without paying an agent, so an outside reader can
# reproduce the tables. These two are transient and are not:
.cache/tmp/
.cache/quarantine/

# The cache is committed VERBATIM: `Store::load` re-derives every entry digest and refuses a
# mismatch, so one file the digest covers but git skipped makes the entry unusable. Measured: the
# rules above excluded 260 Cargo.lock and 8 .cargo/ under .cache, and CI quarantined all 175 entries.
!/.cache/**/.cargo/
!/.cache/**
